<title>INDIA: India Thomas Cook jumps 4.7 pct on bonus meet news.</title>
<headline>India Thomas Cook jumps 4.7 pct on bonus meet news.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Travel and leisure firm Thomas Cook India Ltd shares jumped 4.75 percent after the company said its board will decide on a bonus equity issue on March 17, brokers said.</p>
<p>The share rose 52 rupees to 1,146 at the Bombay Stock Exchange in afternoon trade after starting lower at 1,085.  </p>
<p>The company will also announce its financial results for calendar 1996 on the same day, a Thomas Cook spokeswoman told Reuters on Friday.</p>
<p>The share was up 38.75 rupees, or 3.5 percent, at 1,143.75 on the National Stock Exchange at 0805 GMT.</p>
<p>--Bombay Newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
